From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 02:16:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: macsmc: Use the J713 radio REG_ON action on J604

The MacBook Pro (14-inch, M4) powers its Wi-Fi/Bluetooth module through the
same SMC action as the J713: /amfm function-reg_on is pKW4 on key gP13
with the template argument 0x00800000 in the J604 Apple device tree, as on
J713. m1n1 already drives this rail with that template on both boards
before the kernel starts.

Use the qualified gP13 action on J604 too, so that pcie-apple's
pwren-gpios control uses the same command as the loader instead of a
generic GPIO output, which is not known to be equivalent for this key.

Testing: not yet built; dtc and dtbs_check only.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c
index b9500afad3..4c36748cd0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-macsmc.c
@@ -363,7 +363,8 @@ static int macsmc_gpio_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	smcgp->base_key = data ? data->base_key : _SMC_KEY("gP\0\0");
 	smcgp->j700_pcio = of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j700") &&
 				device_is_compatible(&pdev->dev, "apple,smc-gpio");
-	smcgp->j713 = of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713");
+	smcgp->j713 = of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j713") ||
+		      of_machine_is_compatible("apple,j604");
 	mutex_init(&smcgp->j713_reg_on_lock);
 
 	smcgp->first_index = macsmc_gpio_find_first_gpio_index(smcgp);
